# Accessible Document Style

Write plain prose for later Grade 2 braille. Do not use `*` `(` `)` `&` `#`.

## Headings and lists
BAD: `# Adjectives` or `**Tip:**` or `* identify adjectives` or `- identify adjectives`
GOOD: a title-case or all-caps heading that matches the book, then body text
GOOD: `• identify adjectives`
GOOD: numbered practice `1.` `2.` `3.`
GOOD: `Tip:` `Note:` `FYI:` `Directions:` `Examples` `Caption:`
Keep `Note` on its own line when the book prints it that way.

## Symbols
BAD: `Adjectives & Articles` or `Grade 2 (UEB)` or `#1` or `*(required)*`
GOOD: `Adjectives and Articles`
GOOD: square-bracket asides: `[Themselves reflects winners.]`
GOOD: a section break as `---`
Write "and" not `&`. Avoid parentheses; rephrase or use square brackets.

## Content
Transcribe only what the book says. Possessive apostrophes, hyphens, dashes, and quotation marks are allowed.

After writing, search the file for `*` `(` `)` `&` `#` and rephrase any hit unless the symbol is truly unavoidable in a math or code example.
